---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import PageHero from '../components/ui/PageHero.astro'
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About MOSAIC — what it is, who it serves, and what it is not.">
  <PageHero title="About MOSAIC" subtitle="What MOSAIC is, who it serves, and what we are building together." />

  <div class="container" style="padding-top: var(--space-12); padding-bottom: var(--space-16); max-width: 800px;">

    <section style="margin-bottom: var(--space-12);">
      <h2 style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">What MOSAIC is</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">
        MOSAIC is the shared spatial intelligence network for the CGIAR Multifunctional Landscapes Science Programme — a catalogue and set of connectors that give coherence to the geospatial data produced across CGIAR centres. It is the data discovery and contribution layer for Area of Work 2 — Landscape Optimization &amp; Inclusive Planning. Its guiding principle is to connect, not duplicate: linking to the global data services the world already maintains and combining them with the local datasets only CGIAR holds.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">
        MOSAIC makes it possible to find out what geospatial data exists across the programme, who produced it, at what resolution and time period, and how to access it. Each dataset entry carries a readiness status that tells you how far along the quality control process it is — from first registration through to analytics-ready.
      </p>
      <p>
        MOSAIC is a catalogue, not a file repository. Data files remain hosted by the contributing CGIAR centre and are linked from the catalogue entry. This keeps data ownership and maintenance with the people who know the data best.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: var(--space-12);">
      <h2 style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">Who it serves</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">MOSAIC is built for the CGIAR research community first. In this phase it serves two main groups:</p>
      <ul style="list-style: disc; padding-left: var(--space-6); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-3); color: var(--color-gray-600);">
        <li><strong>Data users</strong> — CGIAR researchers, GIS analysts, and programme staff who need to know what geospatial data exists for a Living Landscape, whether it is available, and how to get it.</li>
        <li><strong>Data contributors</strong> — CGIAR data stewards and centre geospatial focal points who produce datasets for Living Landscapes and want to make them findable, properly documented, and accessible across the programme.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">As the foundations mature, the intent is to open relevant, appropriately licensed parts of MOSAIC to programme partners and to local and national government actors in the landscapes where we work — a deliberate, later phase, not a current commitment.</p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: var(--space-12);">
      <h2 style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">What it is not</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">To keep MOSAIC focused and maintainable, the following are intentionally out of scope for the current release:</p>
      <ul style="list-style: disc; padding-left: var(--space-6); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-3); color: var(--color-gray-600);">
        <li><strong>An interactive map.</strong> Spatial browsing on a map interface is planned for a future release.</li>
        <li><strong>A file upload system.</strong> Datasets are hosted by contributing centres; MOSAIC links to them.</li>
        <li><strong>A centralised data repository.</strong> Data remains with the centres that produced it.</li>
        <li><strong>A real-time data feed.</strong> The catalogue is updated by pull request and rebuilt on every merge.</li>
        <li><strong>User accounts or login.</strong> MOSAIC is fully public and read-only for visitors.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: var(--space-12);">
      <h2 style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">Programme context</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">
        The CGIAR Multifunctional Landscapes (MFL) Science Programme works to restore and sustain landscapes that are simultaneously productive, biodiverse, and resilient. The programme covers flagship Living Landscapes in Kenya, Ethiopia, India, Colombia, and the Mekong region, with a broader network of strategic landscapes.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">
        Area of Work 2 (Landscape Optimization &amp; Inclusive Planning) develops spatially informed approaches to characterize ecosystem condition, identify landscape stress, and support the prioritization of action. MOSAIC is the coordination network that connects this work across centres.
      </p>
      <a href={`${base}/landscapes`} class="btn btn-secondary">View Living Landscapes</a>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: var(--space-12);">
      <h2 style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">Geospatial Community of Practice</h2>
      <p>
        MOSAIC is maintained by the MFL Geospatial Community of Practice, a network of over 230 geospatial specialists and data stewards across CGIAR centres. Focal points in each centre are responsible for registering and validating datasets for their landscapes. If you are a centre focal point and want to contribute data, start at the <a href={`${base}/contribute`}>How to contribute</a> page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">Questions or feedback</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">
        If you have a question about MOSAIC, want to report an error, or are interested in contributing data, use the <a href={`${base}/contact`}>Contact</a> page or open an issue directly on GitHub.
      </p>
      <a href="https://github.com/AoW2-MFL-CGIAR-Science-Program/mfl-living-landscapes-frontend/issues/new/choose" class="btn btn-primary">Open a GitHub Issue</a>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
